# Documentation and ADRs

## ADR format (enforced by CI)

Every ADR in `docs/adr/` must have:
- Frontmatter: `id`, `status`, `scope`
- A `## Verification` section with a command to prove the constraint
- A `## Retirement` section with the condition to remove the rule

Validate: `make validate-adrs`

## Fixture catalog

`docs/FIXTURES.md` tracks verification fixtures with attribution.
When adding a fixture, include: ID, name, type, status, origin (who proposed it).

## Ecosystem docs

Each ecosystem has its own `docs/adr/` directory. ADRs there follow the same format.
